      "_source": "Hair and eyes [S] Sullivan 1921 (Samoa, n=93) and 1922 (Tonga, n=215), Bishop Museum Memoirs 8(2) and 8(4), visual chart observations: black hair 87-94%, no blond, brown eyes 95-100%. Skin [I]: Colmenares et al. 2013 (n=12 Native Hawaiian/Maori/Samoan, back skin) L* 3.8 below Asians in Hawaii; placed between se_asian and south_asian. Low-admixture Polynesians; Native Hawaiians today are ~30% European, ~29% East Asian (Sun et al. 2021)."
